<title>USA: Loewen files $1 bln debt, stock shelf.</title>
<headline>Loewen files $1 bln debt, stock shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loewen Group Inc filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf registration to sell up to $1 billion in debt securities, warrants and preferred and common stock.  </p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for working capital and general corporate purposes, including acquisitions and interest and principal payments on indebtedness, it said.</p>
<p>Loewen, based in Burnaby, British Columbia, Canada, is an operator of funeral homes and cemeteries in North America.</p>
